# Concept B — Mode Toggle

Rail keeps `w-18`. Top toggle switches between Projects view ↔ Tasks view.

## Behavior

- Single icon button at top: switches mode
- **Projects mode** = current rail
- **Tasks mode** = vertical list of task icons (one per active task), grouped by project color stripe on left edge
- Click task icon → open task tab
- Long-press / right-click → context menu (move, archive, etc.)
- Project still selectable via separate dropdown at top in Tasks mode

## Wireframe — Projects mode

```
┌────┐
│ ≡  │
├────┤
│[P]│  ← mode toggle: P=projects
├────┤
│ ⬢ A│
│ ⬡ B│
│ ⬡ C│
│ +  │
├────┤
│ ⚙  │
└────┘
```

## Wireframe — Tasks mode

```
┌────┐
│ ≡  │
├────┤
│[T]│  ← mode toggle: T=tasks
├────┤
│▾All▾  ← project filter dropdown
├────┤
│ ⓘ │  ← task 1 (project A stripe)
│ ⓘ │  ← task 2 (project A)
│ ⓘ │  ← task 3 (project B)
│ ⓘ │  ← task 4 (project C)
│ +  │  ← new task
├────┤
│ ⚙  │
└────┘
```

Each task icon = small avatar/glyph w/ status dot + colored stripe matching project.

## Pros

- Width unchanged → no canvas reflow
- Cheap to implement (swap inner content)
- Tasks become globally browsable

## Cons

- 18px wide = tiny — task labels invisible, only icons + tooltips
- Loss of project switcher in Tasks mode (need filter dropdown)
- Context-switch friction every time user toggle
